<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.ScenarioProgressionDef>
    <defName>Cosmere_Scadrial_Progression_FinalEmpire</defName>
    <label>The Final Empire Progression</label>
    <events>
      <!-- Silent on purpose: no letter. The Final Empire is already under ash when the colony
           lands, and the tracker starts here too. Stated in the def as well so a campaign that
           hands off into this arc from somewhere heavier comes back down to it. -->
      <li>
        <key>ashfall_baseline</key>
        <triggers>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.DaysPassedTrigger">
            <days>0</days>
            <sinceArcStart>true</sinceArcStart>
          </li>
        </triggers>
        <actions>
          <li Class="Cosmere.System.Scadrial.ScenarioPart.Action.SetAshfallIntensityAction">
            <severity>0.15</severity>
          </li>
        </actions>
      </li>
      <li>
        <key>vins_awakening</key>
        <triggers>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.DaysPassedTrigger">
            <days>7</days>
            <sinceArcStart>true</sinceArcStart>
          </li>
        </triggers>
        <actions>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.SendLetterAction">
            <title>Vin's Awakening</title>
            <text>Vin has taken to standing out in it. Not sheltering, not hurrying through - standing, with her arms loose at her sides, letting the mist curl around her until the others stop watching from the doorway and go back to bed. She says it feels like being poured into. Whatever the mists are doing to her, she comes back in steadier than she went out, and the metals answer her faster than they did a week ago.</text>
            <letterDef>PositiveEvent</letterDef>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.SetSkillAction">
            <pawnName>Vin</pawnName>
            <skill>Cosmere_Scadrial_Skill_AllomanticPower</skill>
            <levelOffset>10</levelOffset>
            <passionOffset>1</passionOffset>
          </li>
        </actions>
      </li>
      <li>
        <key>marsh_departure</key>
        <triggers>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.DaysPassedTrigger">
            <days>25</days>
            <sinceArcStart>true</sinceArcStart>
          </li>
        </triggers>
        <actions>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.SendLetterAction">
            <title>Marsh's Infiltration</title>
            <text>Marsh stands at the edge of camp, pack slung over one shoulder. "The Steel Ministry won't infiltrate itself," he says, his voice as flat as ever. Kelsier clasps his brother's arm. No words pass between them - none are needed. Marsh walks into the mists alone. His mission: to become an obligator, to learn the Ministry's secrets from within. It is the most dangerous part of the plan, and the one Marsh insisted on taking.</text>
            <letterDef>NeutralEvent</letterDef>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.RemovePawnAction">
            <pawnName>Marsh</pawnName>
            <!-- leave, not vanish: he is inside the Ministry, not dead, so he stays a world
                 pawn and can come back. -->
            <method>leave</method>
            <optional>true</optional>
          </li>
        </actions>
      </li>
      <li>
        <key>skaa_army</key>
        <triggers>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.DaysPassedTrigger">
            <days>45</days>
            <sinceArcStart>true</sinceArcStart>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.PawnCountTrigger">
            <minCount>8</minCount>
          </li>
        </triggers>
        <actions>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.SendLetterAction">
            <title>The Skaa Rebellion Stirs</title>
            <text>Word has spread through the underground. Yeden's rebels grow bolder by the day, and Ham's training has turned frightened skaa into something resembling soldiers. They march in formation now. They hold their weapons with intent rather than desperation. The numbers are still thin, but the spirit is there - a fire that has not burned on Scadrial in a thousand years.</text>
            <letterDef>PositiveEvent</letterDef>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.SetGoodwillAction">
            <faction>Cosmere_Scadrial_Faction_SkaaRebels</faction>
            <goodwill>75</goodwill>
          </li>
        </actions>
      </li>
      <li>
        <key>kelsiers_sacrifice</key>
        <triggers>
          <!-- Day only. ThreatsSurvivedTrigger reads StoryState.numThreatBigs, which
               Notify_IncidentFired skips for any forced incident, so a dev-fired raid never
               counted towards it and the beat was unreachable outside a full playthrough. -->
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.DaysPassedTrigger">
            <days>60</days>
            <sinceArcStart>true</sinceArcStart>
          </li>
        </triggers>
        <actions>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.ChoiceAction">
            <requiresPawn>Kelsier</requiresPawn>
            <titleKey>CS_Progression_Kelsier_Title</titleKey>
            <textKey>CS_Progression_Kelsier_Text</textKey>
            <acceptKey>CS_Progression_Kelsier_Accept</acceptKey>
            <declineKey>CS_Progression_Kelsier_Decline</declineKey>
            <acceptTipKey>CS_Progression_Kelsier_AcceptTip</acceptTipKey>
            <declineTipKey>CS_Progression_Kelsier_DeclineTip</declineTipKey>
            <onAccept>
              <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.SendLetterAction">
                <title>I Am the One Thing You Can Never Kill</title>
                <text>Kelsier stood before the Steel Inquisitor in the public square. The skaa watched from behind shuttered windows. He fought as only a Mistborn could - iron and steel screaming through the air, pewter fueling impossible strength. But the Inquisitor was stronger. The blow came. Kelsier fell. And then something extraordinary happened. The skaa did not cower. They did not flee. They looked at the body of the Survivor of Hathsin, and they remembered his smile. "I am hope," he had told them. And hope, it turns out, cannot be killed so easily.</text>
                <letterDef>NeutralEvent</letterDef>
              </li>
              <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.RemovePawnAction">
                <pawnName>Kelsier</pawnName>
                <method>leave</method>
                <!-- This branch also runs when he is already dead or gone. -->
                <optional>true</optional>
              </li>
              <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.SetGoodwillAction">
                <faction>Cosmere_Scadrial_Faction_SkaaRebels</faction>
                <goodwill>100</goodwill>
              </li>
              <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.GiveThoughtAction">
                <thought>Cosmere_Scadrial_SurvivorFell</thought>
              </li>
            </onAccept>
            <onDecline>
              <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.SendLetterAction">
                <title>There's Always Another Secret</title>
                <text>Kelsier stopped at the door. Stood there a long moment with his hand on the frame, listening to the Inquisitor call his name across the square. Then he laughed, quietly, and turned back. "Not today," he said. The skaa will not have their martyr. They will have to make do with a living man, which is a harder thing to be.</text>
                <letterDef>NeutralEvent</letterDef>
              </li>
              <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.GiveThoughtAction">
                <thought>Cosmere_Scadrial_EscapedDeath</thought>
                <pawnName>Kelsier</pawnName>
                <permanent>true</permanent>
              </li>
            </onDecline>
          </li>
        </actions>
      </li>
      <li>
        <key>elend_joins</key>
        <triggers>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.DaysPassedTrigger">
            <days>65</days>
            <sinceArcStart>true</sinceArcStart>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.EventOccurredTrigger">
            <eventKey>kelsiers_sacrifice</eventKey>
          </li>
        </triggers>
        <actions>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.TriggerIncidentAction">
            <incident>Cosmere_Scadrial_Incident_ElendArrival</incident>
          </li>
        </actions>
      </li>
      <!-- The loudest beat in the arc. The Ministry comes for the colony in force while Vin
           goes for the Lord Ruler, so the player fights the empire's soldiers on the same night
           somebody else kills its god. The rebellion turns up because they were always going to
           once somebody made the first move. -->
      <li>
        <key>the_collapse</key>
        <triggers>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.DaysPassedTrigger">
            <days>75</days>
            <sinceArcStart>true</sinceArcStart>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.EventOccurredTrigger">
            <eventKey>kelsiers_sacrifice</eventKey>
          </li>
        </triggers>
        <actions>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.SendLetterAction">
            <title>The Collapse</title>
            <text>Vin left before dawn without telling anyone where she was going, which is how everybody knew exactly where she was going.\n\nThe Ministry worked it out too, and they are not chasing her. They are coming here, in strength, to make an example of the place that sheltered the crew - and they have brought everything they had left to bring.\n\nHold the colony. The skaa have been waiting a thousand years for somebody to go first, and word travels faster than soldiers do.</text>
            <letterDef>ThreatBig</letterDef>
          </li>

          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.RemovePawnAction">
            <pawnName>Vin</pawnName>
            <method>leave</method>
            <optional>true</optional>
            <describeKey>CS_Progression_Effect_VinLeaves</describeKey>
          </li>

          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.RaidAction">
            <faction>Cosmere_Scadrial_Faction_FinalEmpireNPC</faction>
            <armyNameKey>CS_Progression_Army_Ministry</armyNameKey>
            <pointsFactor>1.6</pointsFactor>
            <minPoints>2200</minPoints>
            <edge>North</edge>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.RaidAction">
            <faction>Cosmere_Scadrial_Faction_SkaaRebels</faction>
            <armyNameKey>CS_Progression_Army_Rebellion</armyNameKey>
            <friendly>true</friendly>
            <pointsFactor>1.4</pointsFactor>
            <minPoints>1800</minPoints>
            <edge>South</edge>
          </li>
        </actions>
      </li>

      <!-- The morning after. Vin comes back the same pawn who left, because RemovePawnAction
           with "leave" passed her to the world rather than discarding her. -->
      <li>
        <key>the_lord_ruler_falls</key>
        <triggers>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.DaysPassedTrigger">
            <days>77</days>
            <sinceArcStart>true</sinceArcStart>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.EventOccurredTrigger">
            <eventKey>the_collapse</eventKey>
          </li>
        </triggers>
        <actions>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.SendLetterAction">
            <title>He Was Not Immortal After All</title>
            <text>A girl of sixteen, ash-stained and bleeding, pulled the bracers off his arms and he came apart like anybody else.\n\nA thousand years ended in a corridor with nobody watching. By morning the keeps are burning, the Ministry has stopped issuing orders because there is nobody left to issue them, and the skaa are in the streets doing what people do when the thing they were afraid of turns out to have been a man.\n\nWhat comes next has not been decided by anyone, which is the first time that has been true in a thousand years.</text>
            <letterDef>PositiveEvent</letterDef>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.RecallPawnAction">
            <pawnName>Vin</pawnName>
            <letterTitle>She Came Back</letterTitle>
            <letterText>Walked in on her own feet, would not say much, and slept for a day and a half.</letterText>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.SetGoodwillAction">
            <faction>Cosmere_Scadrial_Faction_SkaaRebels</faction>
            <goodwill>100</goodwill>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.GiveThoughtAction">
            <thought>Cosmere_Scadrial_EscapedDeath</thought>
          </li>
          <!-- Both of these end with the empire. The Ministry has nobody left to issue its
               orders, and a rebellion that has won is just people again. -->
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.RemoveFactionAction">
            <factions>
              <li>Cosmere_Scadrial_Faction_FinalEmpireNPC</li>
              <li>Cosmere_Scadrial_Faction_SkaaRebels</li>
            </factions>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.HandOffProgressionAction">
            <progression>Cosmere_Scadrial_Progression_WellOfAscension</progression>
          </li>
        </actions>
      </li>

      <li>
        <key>the_farm</key>
        <triggers>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Trigger.FlagTrigger">
            <flag>HathsinLead</flag>
          </li>
        </triggers>
        <actions>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.SendLetterAction">
            <title>The Seam Was a Splinter</title>
            <text>The survivor talks more freely now that there is atium on the table and none of it went to an obligator. The seam he sent you to was nothing, he says. A crack. The Pits themselves are half a day further in and they are not a mine at all - they are worked, by skaa, under guard, and have been since before anyone's grandfather. That is where the Lord Ruler's atium comes from. All of it.</text>
            <letterDef>NeutralEvent</letterDef>
          </li>
          <li Class="Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.Action.StartQuestAction">
            <questDef>Cosmere_Scadrial_Quest_PitsOfHathsin</questDef>
          </li>
        </actions>
      </li>

    </events>
  </Cosmere.Core.ScenarioPart.ScenarioProgressionDef>
</Defs>
